Package: zzrctsim
Title: Simulation of Longitudinal Randomized Trials with Conditional
    and Marginal Data-Generating Mechanisms
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Ronald G.", family = "Thomas", email = "rgthomas@ucsd.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates longitudinal randomized clinical trials in order
    to evaluate design and analysis choices. A data-generating
    mechanism for a continuous Gaussian outcome may be declared either
    conditionally, through random effects, or marginally, through a
    covariance matrix or a covariance function of time, with exact
    conversion between the two parameterizations where one exists and a
    computable rank certificate where it does not. Visit schedules
    span run-in, treatment and common-close phases, with staggered
    accrual and a common close-out date. Missingness is generated from
    the selection model of Diggle and Kenward (1994)
    <doi:10.2307/2986113>, calibrated to a target dropout proportion,
    with mask generation and mask application kept separate so that
    empirical patterns can be imported; reference-based
    post-discontinuation trajectories are also provided. Simulations
    follow Morris, White and Crowther (2019) <doi:10.1002/sim.8086>:
    'L'Ecuyer-CMRG' substreams with per-replicate state capture,
    performance measures reported with Monte Carlo standard errors, and
    power curves and sample size determination by simulation.
